<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Horatio Nelson</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1758–1805</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Horatio Nelson, 1st Viscount Nelson, Lord Nelson</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Horatio Nelson was a British admiral, the most celebrated naval commander of the Revolutionary and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleonic-wars">Napoleonic Wars</a>. While serving in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-indies">West Indies</a> in the 1780s, he married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frances-nelson-viscountess-nelson">Frances Nisbet</a> on Nevis in 1787. He won the battles of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a> in 1798 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copenhagen">Copenhagen</a> in 1801, and he was killed at the moment of his greatest victory, over the French and Spanish fleets at Trafalgar on 21 October 1805.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/horatio-nelson.jpg" alt="Horatio Nelson" width="320" height="386" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lemuel Francis Abbott · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:HoratioNelson1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
